    "lawCode": "Amd §24, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8829A\n\nSPONSOR: HOYLMAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to the empire state film\nproduction credit\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo allow flexibility within the existing film tax credit to protect\nvariety entertainment shows currently receiving the credit that change\nthe name and/or principal cast of the series.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of this bill allows for variety entertainment shows current-\nly receiving the credit as a continuous production that change the name\nand/or principal cast of the series prior to March 31, 2023, to continue\nreceive the credit if it is filmed in the same location, is produced by\nthe same entity, and retains at least 80% of the staff from the prior\nseason.\n\nSection two provides for an immediate effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nSince 2020, variety entertainment shows are no longer eligible for\nreceiving the New York film tax credit. Any shows in existence at the\ntime were grandfathered in allowing them to continue to receive the\ncredit. This prohibition has been interpretated to mean that successor\nshows cannot receive the credit if the title of the show changes during\na recasting. This narrow view would prevent an existing show from\nrecasting and puts the jobs of the current staff of the show at risk as\nstudios are forced to consider more competitive states. By making this\nminor change an existing show would be able to recast some elements of\ntheir show, but more importantly continue to receive the credit thereby\nprotecting the existing workforce and continuing to film in New York\nwith the associated economic development benefits to its filming\nlocation.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nThere are no fiscal impacts to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nEffective immediately.\n",
