    "memoText": " \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 172\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 8829-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to amend the tax law, in relation to the empire state film\n      production credit\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This legislation would amend the tax  law  to  allow  for  productions\ncurrently receiving the film tax credit to continue to receive the cred-\nit if the name or principal cast of the series changes.\n \n  The film tax credit program was designed to incentivize productions to\nfilm  in  New York and support the creation and retention of jobs in New\nYork. In order to make the program more  strategic  and  sustainable  in\nterms  of  job growth and investment, the State worked with the Legisla-\nture to amend the tax credit to narrow eligibility requirements in 2020.\nThe tax credit does not cover new variety shows, documentaries,  reality\nshows,  or podcasts. While this amendment was implemented, shows already\nin production continued to be eligible for the tax credit.\n \n  This legislation seeks to amend the law to allow a single variety show\nproduction to be eligible for the tax credit, despite the fact  that  it\npost-dates  the  2020 restrictions on eligibility. While I fully support\nefforts to create and retain jobs in our State, to amend the law  for  a\nsingle  production  that does not fall within the credit would undermine\nfairness  in  the  tax  incentive  program.  For  these  reasons,  I  am\nconstrained to veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                       (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
